{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012dAxTqHUqX17sXiiEBGdXh","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! I've read the srd008-ls.yaml file. Here's the full text of the R2 section with requirements R2.1 through R2.6, including the section header and surrounding context:\n\n---\n\n## R2: Filtering, sorting, and metadata display (-a, -A, -d, -t, -S, -r, -U, -v, -i, -s, -n)\n\n**R2.1** - -a must include entries whose names start with \".\" including the special entries \".\" and \"..\" in the listing.\n\n**R2.2** - -A must include entries whose names start with \".\" except for \".\" and \"..\". -A is the \"almost all\" filter.\n\n**R2.3** - -d must list directory entries themselves rather than their contents. When a directory is given as an argument with -d, must print the directory name (or its long-format entry with -l) without descending into it.\n\n**R2.4** - When both -a and -A are given, the last one on the command line takes precedence, matching GNU ls behavior.\n\n**R2.5** - -t must sort entries by modification time, newest first. Obtain metadata via pkg/sys.Lstat(path string) (*sys.FileInfo, error); use sys.FileInfo.ModTime time.Time for comparison (fi.ModTime.After(fj.ModTime) for newest-first ordering). Entries with the same modification time must be sorted by name in C locale order as a tiebreaker.\n\n**R2.6** - -S must sort entries by file size (st_size), largest first. Obtain file size from sys.FileInfo.Size int64 — apparent file size in bytes (st_size). Entries with the same size must be sorted by name in C locale order as a tiebreaker.\n\n---\n\nThe progression shows:\n- **R2.1 & R2.2** establish the baseline filter behaviors (show/hide dotfiles)\n- **R2.3 & R2.4** extend filtering with the -d flag and precedence rules for conflicting flags\n- **R2.5 & R2.6** introduce sorting by metadata (modification time and file size), each with name-based tiebreakers"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"98b2423d-f7e4-4d63-a55b-b140133c07a5","uuid":"79ac9399-1f57-4558-93bf-9a314f5f03cf","timestamp":"2026-05-14T21:38:26.359Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"I need to find and read the requirements R2.3, R2.4, R2.5, and R2.6 from the srd008-ls SRD. The file should be at docs/specs/software-requirements/srd008-ls.yaml. Read that file and extract the full text of requirements R2.3 through R2.6 (and any surrounding context like the R2 section header). Also provide context on R2.1 and R2.2 so I understand the progression. Report the full text of each requirement.","agentId":"a54a3abaed6a2e395","agentType":"Explore","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! I've read the srd008-ls.yaml file. Here's the full text of the R2 section with requirements R2.1 through R2.6, including the section header and surrounding context:\n\n---\n\n## R2: Filtering, sorting, and metadata display (-a, -A, -d, -t, -S, -r, -U, -v, -i, -s, -n)\n\n**R2.1** - -a must include entries whose names start with \".\" including the special entries \".\" and \"..\" in the listing.\n\n**R2.2** - -A must include entries whose names start with \".\" except for \".\" and \"..\". -A is the \"almost all\" filter.\n\n**R2.3** - -d must list directory entries themselves rather than their contents. When a directory is given as an argument with -d, must print the directory name (or its long-format entry with -l) without descending into it.\n\n**R2.4** - When both -a and -A are given, the last one on the command line takes precedence, matching GNU ls behavior.\n\n**R2.5** - -t must sort entries by modification time, newest first. Obtain metadata via pkg/sys.Lstat(path string) (*sys.FileInfo, error); use sys.FileInfo.ModTime time.Time for comparison (fi.ModTime.After(fj.ModTime) for newest-first ordering). Entries with the same modification time must be sorted by name in C locale order as a tiebreaker.\n\n**R2.6** - -S must sort entries by file size (st_size), largest first. Obtain file size from sys.FileInfo.Size int64 — apparent file size in bytes (st_size). Entries with the same size must be sorted by name in C locale order as a tiebreaker.\n\n---\n\nThe progression shows:\n- **R2.1 & R2.2** establish the baseline filter behaviors (show/hide dotfiles)\n- **R2.3 & R2.4** extend filtering with the -d flag and precedence rules for conflicting flags\n- **R2.5 & R2.6** introduce sorting by metadata (modification time and file size), each with name-based tiebreakers"}],"totalDurationMs":8784,"totalTokens":26478,"totalToolUseCount":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":5,"cache_creation_input_tokens":9829,"cache_read_input_tokens":16123,"output_tokens":521,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":9829},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":5,"output_tokens":521,"cache_read_input_tokens":16123,"cache_creation_input_tokens":9829,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":9829,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"toolStats":{"readCount":1,"searchCount":0,"bashCount":0,"editFileCount":0,"linesAdded":0,"linesRemoved":0,"otherToolCount":0}}}
